What you may do:

1. Use the app. You may use SVGcinema as published by the copyright holder (for example at
   https://asafco83.github.io/svgcinema/) to create, save and export animations.

2. Use your exported files. The files you export from SVGcinema (such as animated SVG files) are
   yours to use, copy, distribute and sell for any purpose, including commercial purposes. This
   includes the parts of the Software that SVGcinema puts into those files (the animation
   player), as part of those files only.

3. Use the external player. Exported files can rely on the SVGcinema player file
   (cin-player.min.js, published as the npm package "svgcinema-player") instead of carrying the
   player inside them. You may load that file from a public content delivery network such as
   jsDelivr, and you may copy and host unmodified copies of it on your own servers, for the sole
   purpose of playing files exported from SVGcinema. You may not modify it, or use or distribute
   it for any other purpose.

4. View the repository. While the repository is public on GitHub, you may view it and fork it on
   GitHub as GitHub's Terms of Service allow. That gives you no other rights to the Software.

